Set-Location -LiteralPath $PSScriptRoot
$msg = 'workspaces: a brand is now a place you can stand, and God Mode has a real doorway. God Mode rail carried ONE workspace jump straight to /sales with the brand named in a literal - EvoSys Pro brand sales - and /sales takes no brand parameter, returning EVERY brand sales org for a god_admin. With one brand seeded that looked like a sensible default; the day a second brand existed it would have blended two companies pipelines onto one screen under one brand name, silently. Adds the missing middle level. X-Brand-Override travels like X-Org-Override - god only, request scoped, never persisted, validated against a real platform row - with selected_brand_id and a brand_write_platform_id guard beside the existing tenant one. POST /god/platform/context/brand/{id} mirrors enter_customer exactly, audited and asserting memberships_before equals memberships_after, because entering a brand is administrative visibility and not employment. _resolved_context now emits THREE levels rather than two, plus a server decided breadcrumb trail so every client says AdvisorFlow then EvoSys Pro then Restland identically, and neutral now means nothing selected rather than merely no customer. The load bearing change: a selected brand NARROWS sales_org_ids to that brand sales orgs and never widens, while a neutral owner still sees every brand so nothing was taken away. New Workspaces page driven entirely by the platform records - brands from the overview endpoint, customers from the per brand endpoint, each rendered in its own accent and mark from the columns consolidated yesterday, and no brand named anywhere in the code, so a future brand appears in the doorway the moment its row exists. ContextBanner renders the server trail with Switch workspace and Return to God Mode. Closes the implicit context creations: POST /admin/users read current_user.organization_id directly and for a neutral owner that is None, and an org NULL user is the systems positive assertion of a brand sales identity - so creating a user from God Mode with nothing selected manufactured a phantom seller holding no membership, refused by every tenant route. It and the two nullable proposal writes now go through tenant_write_org_id and return a 409 naming the context to select. Of the 33 direct attribution sites only 2 could create an ownerless row; 16 write a NOT NULL column and fail loudly, and the rest are audit or service calls - measured rather than assumed after a first pass regex read nullability wrongly. God cross platform access, same brand super_admin access and customer isolation all re asserted.'
& "$PSScriptRoot\deploy.ps1" -Message $msg
Write-Output ("DEPLOY_EXIT=" + $LASTEXITCODE)
